<!-- SECTION 4: WHO NEEDS THIS -->
<section class="content-section" id="who-section">
    <div class="content-container">
        <div class="text-content">
                <h2 class="section-title" id="who-needs-section">Who Needs GSTAT Appeal Filing at the Kochi Bench</h2><p>Any registered taxpayer or GST-registered business in Kerala or Lakshadweep that has received an unfavourable order from the First Appellate Authority under Section 107 or the Revisional Authority under Section 108 of the CGST/KGST Act can file a second appeal before the Kochi GSTAT Bench or Thiruvananthapuram circuit under Section 112.</p><h3>Thiruvananthapuram Circuit Bench</h3><p>If your business is registered in Thiruvananthapuram, Kollam, Alappuzha, Pathanamthitta, or Kottayam, your GSTAT appeal is filed at the Thiruvananthapuram circuit bench, not directly at Kochi (Ernakulam). Patron's team handles routing and filing at both locations. See also <a href="/gstat-appeal-filing/chennai">GSTAT appeal filing in Chennai</a> and <a href="#">GSTAT appeal filing in Bangalore</a> for neighbouring state benches.</p><h3>Common Demand Categories in Kerala</h3><ul><li>Services sector ITC disputes - IT/ITES companies in Infopark Kochi, SmartCity, and Technopark Thiruvananthapuram</li><li>Spice export classification and valuation disputes from the Kochi spice market</li><li>Tourism and hospitality disputes - restaurant service rates, hotel accommodation, houseboat classification in Alappuzha</li><li>Rubber and plantation product classification from the Kottayam-Idukki belt</li><li>Coir industry classification disputes from Alappuzha, seafood export refund claims from Kozhikode</li><li>E-way bill violations and retail sector penalty orders across Kerala</li><li>Adverse orders on <a href="/gst-notice">GST notice</a> responses requiring tribunal appeal</li></ul>
            </div>
    </div>
</section>

<!-- SECTION 5: OUR SERVICES -->
<section class="content-section" id="services-section">
    <div class="content-container">
        <div class="text-content">
                <h2 class="section-title" id="services-section">GSTAT Appeal Filing Services at Kochi Bench</h2><div class="table-responsive-wrapper"><table><thead><tr><th>Service</th><th>What We Do</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>Appealability Assessment</td><td>Review demand order from CGST Kochi, Thiruvananthapuram, or Kozhikode Commissionerate or KGST Commissioner. Determine Kochi main bench or Thiruvananthapuram circuit routing.</td></tr><tr><td>Pre-deposit Computation</td><td>Strategic computation of 20% under S.112(8). For Lakshadweep, UTGST applies. Hardship waiver guidance for SME spice and coir sectors.</td></tr><tr><td>Form APL-05 Drafting</td><td>Draft grounds specific to spice classification, IT services ITC, tourism sector rates, and rubber product HSN disputes. Malayalam order translation coordination.</td></tr><tr><td>E-Filing Portal Navigation</td><td>End-to-end filing on <a href="https://efiling.gstat.gov.in" target="_blank" rel="noopener">efiling.gstat.gov.in</a>. Correct routing between Kochi main bench and Thiruvananthapuram circuit.</td></tr><tr><td>Bench Appearance (Kochi)</td><td>Of-counsel GST litigation specialists attend admission, stay, and final arguments at the Kochi main bench.</td></tr><tr><td>Bench Appearance (Thiruvananthapuram Circuit)</td><td>Coordinate hearings at the Thiruvananthapuram circuit for 5 southern Kerala districts.</td></tr><tr><td>Malayalam Translation Coordination</td><td>Arrange certified English translations of Malayalam-language orders from Kerala State GST authorities.</td></tr><tr><td>Post-Order Advisory</td><td>Analyse GSTAT order, advise on appeal to Kerala HC at Ernakulam under S.113 - co-located with GSTAT bench.</td></tr></tbody></table></div>
