<!-- SECTION 7: STEP-BY-STEP PROCESS -->
<section class="steps-section" id="procedure-section">
    <div class="section-container">
        <header class="section-header" style="text-align:center;margin-bottom:48px;">
            <span class="section-eyebrow"><svg viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" style="width:18px;height:18px;"><circle cx="12" cy="12" r="10"/><polyline points="12 6 12 12 16 14"/></svg> Our Process</span>
            <h2 class="section-title">GSTAT Appeal Filing Process at Kochi Bench - 6 Steps</h2>
            <p>Follow this step-by-step process. Patron Accounting's CA team manages every stage at both Kochi bench and Thiruvananthapuram circuit.</p>
        </header>
        <div class="steps-container">
            <div class="step-card">
    <div class="step-content"><span class="step-badge">Step 1</span><h3 class="step-title">Assess Appealability</h3><p class="step-description">Verify the demand order from the CGST Commissionerate Kochi, Thiruvananthapuram, or Kozhikode, or the Commissioner of Commercial Taxes (KGST), Kerala is appealable under S.112. Determine whether filing is at the Kochi main bench or Thiruvananthapuram circuit based on your district of registration. For Lakshadweep businesses, verify the CGST or UTGST authority.</p><div class="step-highlights"><span class="highlight-tag"><svg viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2"><polyline points="20 6 9 17 4 12"/></svg>Verify S.112 grounds</span><span class="highlight-tag"><svg viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2"><polyline points="20 6 9 17 4 12"/></svg>Kochi vs TVM circuit routing</span></div></div>
    <div class="step-visual"><div class="step-illustration"><div class="illustration-icon"><svg viewBox="0 0 120 100" fill="none" xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg"><rect x="15" y="5" width="90" height="70" rx="6" fill="#F0F4F8" stroke="#14365F" stroke-width="1.5"/><line x1="30" y1="25" x2="90" y2="25" stroke="#F5A623" stroke-width="3" stroke-linecap="round"/><line x1="30" y1="40" x2="80" y2="40" stroke="#14365F" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" opacity="0.3"/><line x1="30" y1="52" x2="70" y2="52" stroke="#14365F" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" opacity="0.3"/><circle cx="80" cy="60" r="12" fill="#E8712C" opacity="0.15"/><path d="M76 60l3 3 6-6" stroke="#E8712C" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round"/></svg></div><span class="illustration-label">Order Review</span><span class="step-number-large">01</span></div></div>
</div>
<div class="step-card" style="direction:rtl">
    <div class="step-content" style="direction:ltr"><span class="step-badge">Step 2</span><h3 class="step-title">Calculate Pre-deposit</h3><p class="step-description">Compute 20% of disputed tax under S.112(8). Cumulative: 10% from first appeal + 10% for GSTAT. Cap: Rs 20 crore each CGST and SGST (or UTGST for Lakshadweep). For penalty-only demands under KGST Act, 10%. Payment through Electronic Cash Ledger.</p><div class="step-highlights"><span class="highlight-tag"><svg viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2"><polyline points="20 6 9 17 4 12"/></svg>20% cumulative</span><span class="highlight-tag"><svg viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2"><polyline points="20 6 9 17 4 12"/></svg>UTGST for Lakshadweep</span></div></div>
    <div class="step-visual" style="direction:ltr"><div class="step-illustration"><div class="illustration-icon"><svg viewBox="0 0 120 100" fill="none" xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg"><rect x="15" y="5" width="90" height="70" rx="6" fill="#F0F4F8" stroke="#14365F" stroke-width="1.5"/><line x1="30" y1="25" x2="90" y2="25" stroke="#F5A623" stroke-width="3" stroke-linecap="round"/><line x1="30" y1="40" x2="80" y2="40" stroke="#14365F" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" opacity="0.3"/><line x1="30" y1="52" x2="70" y2="52" stroke="#14365F" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" opacity="0.3"/><circle cx="80" cy="60" r="12" fill="#E8712C" opacity="0.15"/><path d="M76 60l3 3 6-6" stroke="#E8712C" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round"/></svg></div><span class="illustration-label">Pre-deposit Paid</span><span class="step-number-large">02</span></div></div>
</div>
<div class="step-card">
    <div class="step-content"><span class="step-badge">Step 3</span><h3 class="step-title">Prepare Form APL-05</h3><p class="step-description">Draft grounds of appeal with consecutively numbered paragraphs. Kerala matters often involve spice classification, IT services ITC, tourism sector rates, and rubber product HSN disputes. Compile documents, obtain certified copies. Malayalam-language orders require English translation. GSTAT offline Excel utility generates JSON for upload.</p><div class="step-highlights"><span class="highlight-tag"><svg viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2"><polyline points="20 6 9 17 4 12"/></svg>Sector-specific grounds</span><span class="highlight-tag"><svg viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2"><polyline points="20 6 9 17 4 12"/></svg>Malayalam translation if needed</span></div></div>
    <div class="step-visual"><div class="step-illustration"><div class="illustration-icon"><svg viewBox="0 0 120 100" fill="none" xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg"><rect x="15" y="5" width="90" height="70" rx="6" fill="#F0F4F8" stroke="#14365F" stroke-width="1.5"/><line x1="30" y1="25" x2="90" y2="25" stroke="#F5A623" stroke-width="3" stroke-linecap="round"/><line x1="30" y1="40" x2="80" y2="40" stroke="#14365F" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" opacity="0.3"/><line x1="30" y1="52" x2="70" y2="52" stroke="#14365F" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" opacity="0.3"/><circle cx="80" cy="60" r="12" fill="#E8712C" opacity="0.15"/><path d="M76 60l3 3 6-6" stroke="#E8712C" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round"/></svg></div><span class="illustration-label">APL-05 Ready</span><span class="step-number-large">03</span></div></div>
</div>
<div class="step-card" style="direction:rtl">
    <div class="step-content" style="direction:ltr"><span class="step-badge">Step 4</span><h3 class="step-title">File on GSTAT E-Filing Portal</h3><p class="step-description">Submit Form APL-05 at <a href="https://efiling.gstat.gov.in" target="_blank" rel="noopener">efiling.gstat.gov.in</a> with pre-deposit proof within 3 months under S.112(1). Ensure correct routing - businesses in 5 southern districts file at Thiruvananthapuram circuit, others at Kochi main bench. Backlog: deadline 30 June 2026.</p><div class="step-highlights"><span class="highlight-tag"><svg viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2"><polyline points="20 6 9 17 4 12"/></svg>3-month limitation</span><span class="highlight-tag"><svg viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2"><polyline points="20 6 9 17 4 12"/></svg>Correct circuit routing</span></div></div>
    <div class="step-visual" style="direction:ltr"><div class="step-illustration"><div class="illustration-icon"><svg viewBox="0 0 120 100" fill="none" xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg"><rect x="15" y="5" width="90" height="70" rx="6" fill="#F0F4F8" stroke="#14365F" stroke-width="1.5"/><line x1="30" y1="25" x2="90" y2="25" stroke="#F5A623" stroke-width="3" stroke-linecap="round"/><line x1="30" y1="40" x2="80" y2="40" stroke="#14365F" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" opacity="0.3"/><line x1="30" y1="52" x2="70" y2="52" stroke="#14365F" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" opacity="0.3"/><circle cx="80" cy="60" r="12" fill="#E8712C" opacity="0.15"/><path d="M76 60l3 3 6-6" stroke="#E8712C" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round"/></svg></div><span class="illustration-label">E-Filed</span><span class="step-number-large">04</span></div></div>
</div>
<div class="step-card">
    <div class="step-content"><span class="step-badge">Step 5</span><h3 class="step-title">Attend Admission Hearing</h3><p class="step-description">Patron's of-counsel GST litigation specialists with 15+ years of indirect tax experience appear at the Kochi bench or Thiruvananthapuram circuit. Hybrid mode - physical and video conferencing. Businesses in Wayanad, Kasaragod, and Lakshadweep can attend via video conferencing.</p><div class="step-highlights"><span class="highlight-tag"><svg viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2"><polyline points="20 6 9 17 4 12"/></svg>Hybrid hearing mode</span><span class="highlight-tag"><svg viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2"><polyline points="20 6 9 17 4 12"/></svg>Both locations covered</span></div></div>
