<!-- SECTION 18: URGENCY CTA -->
<section class="content-section" style="background: var(--orange-lighter) !important; border-left: 4px solid var(--orange);">
    <div class="content-container">
        <div class="text-content">
            <div class="content-text">
                <h2 class="section-title" style="color:var(--orange) !important;">Why You Must Act Now for Your Kochi GSTAT Appeal</h2><div class="highlight-box" style="background:#FEF2F2;border-left:4px solid #EF4444;padding:20px 24px;border-radius:var(--radius-md);margin-bottom:20px;"><p style="font-weight:700;color:#991B1B;margin-bottom:4px;">Statutory Time Bar - Not Negotiable</p><p>The 3-month limitation under S.112(1) CGST/KGST Act permanently extinguishes the right of appeal. Condonation under S.112(4) is discretionary.</p></div><p>For Kerala and Lakshadweep businesses with orders before 1 April 2026, the backlog deadline is 30 June 2026. Kerala's high consumer spending economy and active GST enforcement will generate significant filing volumes at both Kochi bench and Thiruvananthapuram circuit.</p><p>Every day of delay compounds interest. The bench is newly operational - early filers benefit from shorter queues.</p><p style="font-weight:700;font-size:18px;margin-top:20px;">Contact Patron's team today: <a href="tel:+919459456700">+91 945 945 6700</a> | <a href="https://wa.me/919459456700?text=Hello%2C%20I%20just%20visited%20your%20GSTAT%20Appeal%20Filing%20in%20Kochi%20page.%20I%20would%20like%20to%20know%20more%20about%20it." target="_blank" rel="noopener">WhatsApp</a></p>
